course: dictionary
lesson: 14409
title: Overeat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The prefix over- means too much, so overeat means to eat too much food, more than your body needs. «On her birthday, Maya tried to overeat cake and crisps, and by bedtime her tummy hurt.» The words tummy hurt are a clue that eating too much can make you feel unwell.
explain: Overeat is a verb with several forms: «He overeats at every party», «Yesterday I overate», and «I have overeaten.» Overeating is the -ing form, the name for the action. To check a meaning, swap in «eat more than you need» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Health lessons teach that eating slowly helps you notice when you are full. «Dad said, "Eat slowly, so you notice when you are full."» Holidays and parties are times when people often overeat, so it is useful to stop when you feel full.
fact: Overeat is a verb: overeat, overeats, overate, overeaten, overeating.
fact: The prefix over- means too much, so overeat means eat too much.
fact: «Overeat» means to eat more food than your body needs.
fact: Overeating, especially sweets and fatty food, can make you feel sick.
fact: Eating slowly helps you notice when you are full.
exercise: «Maya tried to overeat cake and crisps at her birthday party.» What does overeat mean? | To sleep after dinner | To cook food for a long time | *To eat more food than your body needs | To pass food to a friend
exercise: The word «overeat» has the prefix over-. What does over- mean here? | Half | *Too much | Not at all | Very quickly
exercise: Complete the sentence: «Yesterday I ___ too many sweets.» | overeating | overeat | overeats | *overate
test: «After the feast, Sam felt sick because he had overeaten.» What does overeaten mean here? | Cooked a feast for everyone | Lost his appetite for ever | *Eaten more than his body needed | Gone to bed early
test: Dad says, «Eat slowly.» Why? | *To help you notice when you are full | To be the first to finish | To make the food last less | To eat in silence
exam: Which is a good way to avoid overeating? | Keep eating until the plate is empty, even when you are full | Eat as fast as you can | Skip every meal in the day | *Stop eating when you notice you are full
